---
// The overview index idiom, device 6 of 8: the section's terms, in the callout
// idiom the archetypes already own (specs/design/palette.md §7.3). Not an
// apology, and not about emptiness. See IndexHeader.astro for the family
// rationale.
//
// It renders in the empty state on all three indexes, and each one says
// something different: /writing/ states what belongs and what does not,
// /he/writing/ states the licence condition, /projects/ gets one line because
// on that page the callout is a formality. Same device, three sets of terms —
// a slot, not a prop.
//
// ── the two temperatures ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// `[data-theme='warm'] .terms` was the only theme-conditional rule in the
// stylesheet, and it is the first use of the `warm:` custom variant that
// global.css declares as `([data-theme='warm'] &)`. It compiles to
// `[data-theme='warm'] .warm\:bg-badge-2`, which is the original selector with
// a different class name in it — same descendant shape, same two-class
// specificity, so it beats the resting `bg-surface-inset` on specificity and
// not on emit order. That distinction is the point: this pair is the one place
// in the family where two fills target one element, and it resolves the way
// the stylesheet did rather than the way Tailwind's sort happens to fall.
//
// The attribute is on <html>, set before first paint by the inline script in
// Base.astro, so the variant is a plain ancestor match with nothing to
// coordinate.
//
// ── the edges ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// `padding: 20px 24px` is 20px on the block axis and 24px on the inline one,
// which is `pbs-5 pbe-5 ps-6 pe-6` and not the other way round.
//
// The 3px accent edge is `border-inline-start`, so under /he/writing/'s
// dir="rtl" it draws on the right, where the reading starts. `border-l-` would
// have put it on the left on both pages and nothing would have failed.
//
// `[&>*+*]:mbs-3` is the `.terms > * + *` rule: 12px between the paragraphs,
// none above the first, and the callout does not care how many there are.
---

<div
  class="mbs-10 pbs-5 pbe-5 ps-6 pe-6 bg-surface-inset warm:bg-badge-2 border-s-[3px] border-s-accent-2 rounded-(--radius-s) text-size-meta leading-body text-muted max-inline-[64ch] [&>*+*]:mbs-3"
>
  <slot />
</div>
